Like Topi said, water walking boots are guaranteed in Vlad's Tower.
The only trouble is that you can't flee back up to safety (such as it
is) without going quite far into Gehennom.  Also, keep in mind that
you vaporized the items that would likely have gotten you over the
water.  Normally, the game generates sufficient tools to get past the
water on Medusa's level, with sufficient creativity.

As long as you are not playing a pacifist, one can eventually get any
item ("some exceptions apply, consult store for details") via death
drops.  It's kind of weird to kill a giant beetle and have it drop
Cleaver, but it happens, or more commonly, kill a black pudding and
find a ring.

Also, the wand of wishing and the castle armory are below Medusa and
can help you cross water.  Depending on how daring I am feeling, or
how much of a packrat I am being, I will just dig down through Medusa
and worry about how to cross later.


